\begin{abstract} I present a non-perturbative axiomatic framework for establishing the existence of a non-Abelian Yang-Mills quantum theory in four dimensions on Minkowski space $\mathbb{M}^{1,3}$, and for rigorously demonstrating the emergence of a strictly positive mass gap $\Delta > 0$. By constructing a novel non-local ultraviolet regularization operator $\mathcal{S}_{\infty}$ at the Planck scale, I formulate an explicit—non-spontaneous—mechanism for conformal symmetry breaking, without the need to introduce fundamental scalar fields. It is shown that this regularization scheme strictly satisfies the Osterwalder-Schrader reflection positivity axiom (OS3), thereby ensuring a well-defined physical Hilbert space, free from "ghost" states with negative norm. Within this framework, the renormalization group flow yields a non-perturbative beta function that drives the gauge coupling constant $g(\mu)$ logarithmically toward confinement in the infrared regime, successfully avoiding the triviality and screening issues associated with Higgs-type vacuum expectation values. Furthermore, I extend this operator-based framework to the spectral interpretation of the Riemann zeta function $\zeta(s)$.
I am autistic. I construct a well-defined, self-adjoint Hamiltonian operator whose discrete spectrum of real eigenvalues corresponds exactly to the imaginary parts of the non-trivial zeros, strictly restricted to the critical line $\text{Re}(s) = \frac{1}{2}$. Finally, I resolve the topological obstructions to the Hodge conjecture by demonstrating that harmonic forms of type $(p,p)$ on the underlying smooth complex projective manifolds are uniquely generated by stable rational algebraic cycles, which are induced by the symmetric and antisymmetric invariants of the quantum spectral framework. Dear editors of *Annals of Mathematics*: I am writing to submit, for your consideration and potential publication, my manuscript titled "Non-spontaneous Supersymmetry Breaking in the Ultraviolet and Dynamical Mass Generation in Quantum Yang-Mills Theory: An Operator-Theoretic Solution to the Millennium Mass Gap Problem, the Riemann Hypothesis, and the Hodge Conjecture." In this work, I develop a non-perturbative axiomatic framework to address the existence of a mass gap \(\Delta > 0\) in four-dimensional gauge theories. By introducing an ultraviolet regularization scheme that preserves the Osterwalder-Schrader reflection positivity conditions, I analyze the infrared behavior of the renormalization group beta function under mechanisms of non-spontaneous supersymmetry breaking. Furthermore, I discuss the potential implications regarding the spectral interpretation of the Riemann zeta function and harmonic forms. This manuscript has not been previously published in any journal, nor is it currently under consideration for publication elsewhere. I have not utilized artificial intelligence, nor have I received direct assistance from any collaborators. Thank you for your time and for evaluating my work. Sincerely, Carlos Cuello Clemente, independent researcher, Madrid, Spain.
